course: dictionary
lesson: 12980
title: Wide open spaces
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An expanse is a very wide, open area of land, sea, sky or something else. When you meet this word, look for clues in the sentence. «From the top of the hill, we saw a wide expanse of blue sea.» The word wide tells you the sea spreads far in every direction.
explain: Writers often use expanse to describe places that seem to go on and on. «The desert is a huge expanse of sand.» Huge and sand are the clues: the desert is very big, and it is covered in sand.
explain: The word can also describe things that are not places. «The sky was an endless expanse of grey.» Here the sky is not a place you can walk across, but it still stretches far, so expanse fits. Check by swapping in a simple word: a wide area of grey sky makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: An expanse is a very wide, open area of land, sea, sky or something else.
fact: The plural of expanse is expanses.
fact: An expanse suggests something large, smooth or empty, stretching out far.
fact: «Vast» and «wide» are good clue words, because they show that an expanse is very big.
fact: Expanse is often used in descriptions of deserts, oceans, snow and the sky.
exercise: «From the top of the hill, we saw a wide expanse of blue sea.» What does expanse mean? | A tiny stream | A loud noise | A small wooden bench | *A very wide, open area
exercise: «The desert is a huge expanse of sand.» Which word in this sentence tells you the expanse is very big? | *huge | desert | the | sand
exercise: «The sky was an endless expanse of grey.» What does expanse suggest here? | *Something large and empty, stretching far | Something tiny and crowded | Something hot and sticky | Something that makes a loud sound
test: «The plane flew over an expanse of snow.» Which word is closest in meaning to expanse? | noise | shoe | cup | *area
test: Which of these is an expanse? | A pencil case | A small button | A single raindrop | *An open sea stretching to the horizon
exam: Mia says, «The ocean is a vast expanse.» What does expanse mean here? | A type of cake | A narrow crack in a wall | A quick shout | *A very wide, open stretch of water
